sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0243/0244 task, DECISIONS R1-R4, agent-observer-swamp-acts, single-swamp-node. docs/reference/node-provisioning.md#converge-the-orbit-footprint.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: node:converge
  %% kind: node.converge
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Target Node<br/>reached over ssh
  CLI->>GW: node:converge 12<br/>--force
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit node:converge 12 --force`
  %%> - syntax: `<node> [--force] [--idempotency-key=KEY] [--json]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the Node, by id or exact name
  %%> - `--force` re-applies every part, not only the parts whose digest changed
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - re-applies Orbit's own files on Node 12: the Node agent, the private DNS client policy, and the files of its active roles
  %%> - never changes an Instance, a Process, a Schedule or a role assignment, so it is safe on a Node that owns Instances
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - the `orbit` CLI, the MCP tool, and the fleet rollout send the same request
  Note over GW: Render the footprint<br/>task #5132 · digest per part
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to Node 12
  %%> - Node 12 is an active, managed Linux Node
  %%> - no other converge or Node agent rekey runs for Node 12; the Gateway holds one lock per Node
  %%> Builds:
  %%> - the pinned `orbit-agent` release and its SHA-256
  %%> - the Node agent configuration, Orbit root certificate and unit
  %%> - the private DNS client policy, when Node 12 is a peer with roles
  %%> Refuses:
  %%> - a part the Gateway cannot render, before any run starts
  %%> - the files of each active role, through the shared role steps
  %%> - one digest per part, from the Gateway's own code and pins; no SSH
  %%> Result:
  %%> - task #5132 recorded with the full intent and the parts to apply
  %%> - unchanged parts are left out, unless `--force`
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-node-converge
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209)
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - the parts to apply, with their files and digests
  %%> - the agent's verifier hash, to check the existing key; never the key
  %%> - Node 12's address and SSH host keys; the SSH identity comes from the `swamp` role
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5132
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
  SW->>N: Install the Node agent<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/fetch · sha256
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - downloads the pinned `orbit-agent` release to `/usr/local/bin/orbit-agent` and checks its SHA-256
  %%> - a binary that already matches the pin is left alone
  %%> How:
  %%> - the official `@swamp/cfgmgmt/fetch` behavior over SSH from 209, with sudo
  %%> - no `orbit-agent command …`; the agent only observes and runs no actions
  SW->>N: Configure the Node agent<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/file
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - writes `config.toml` and `ca.pem` in `/etc/orbit/agent`, one official `file` behavior each
  %%> Keeps the key:
  %%> - never writes `/etc/orbit/agent/secret`; the end check compares it with the recorded verifier
  SW->>N: Start the Node agent<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/systemd apply
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - writes the `orbit-agent.service` unit the Gateway rendered, with access to the apps root, then enables and starts it
  SW->>N: Restart the Node agent<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/systemd restart
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - restarts the agent so it reads its new binary and files
  %%> Why always:
  %%> - this part only runs when its digest changed, or with `--force`
  SW->>N: Close Instance .env files<br/>@swamp/ssh exec · find
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - removes the world bits from `.env` in each Instance checkout under the apps root, in one `find`
  %%> On failure:
  %%> - best effort: a checkout that is gone does not fail the converge
  opt Node 12 is a DNS peer
    SW->>N: Apply private DNS policy<br/>resolver for .orbit domains
    %%> When:
    %%> - Node 12 is an active managed peer with roles; not the `vpn` Node and not the Gateway's Node
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - sends the private `.orbit` domains to the Orbit DNS server, with the split DNS policy
    %%> - no WireGuard tunnel restart
  end
  opt Node 12 has active roles
    SW->>N: Install Caddy<br/>cfgmgmt fetch · exec floor
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - downloads the pinned Caddy package with `@swamp/cfgmgmt/fetch`, checked against its SHA-256
    %%> - installs it with `@swamp/cfgmgmt/exec`, unless the installed Caddy already meets the version floor
    %%> - proves the floor with `dpkg --compare-versions`
    %%> For:
    %%> - a Caddy role or Caddy sites
    %%> Every role part:
    %%> - runs only when its digest changed or with `--force`
    %%> - runs beside the other parts; one part's failure never stops another
    SW->>N: Publish Caddy sites<br/>cfgmgmt file · validate · reload
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - writes the rendered Caddyfile as a candidate, validates it as the `caddy` user, publishes it with the Routes Caddy step, and removes the candidate
    %%> - a Caddyfile Caddy refuses fails this part; the published Caddyfile stays
    %%> - a Caddyfile the Gateway could not render is skipped and reported
    SW->>N: Install private DNS<br/>cfgmgmt file · systemd · assert
    %%> For:
    %%> - a `vpn` Node that publishes private DNS
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - writes the listener release files, self-tests the release, then writes the socket and service units with `@swamp/cfgmgmt/systemd`
    %%> - writes the dnsmasq records and the catalog, tests dnsmasq, restarts it and the listener
    %%> - asserts that the listener loaded the new catalog
    %%> No rollback:
    %%> - a failed check leaves the new files; a rerun repairs them
    SW->>N: Configure PHP-FPM<br/>per version · cfgmgmt · reload
    %%> For:
    %%> - `app-dev` and `app-prod`, once per PHP version; a version without PHP-FPM is skipped
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - writes Orbit's runtime settings, links them into PHP-FPM, sets the master's stop timeout, tests the configuration and reloads the running masters
    SW->>N: Write the tmpfiles rule<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/file
    %%> For:
    %%> - `app-dev`: the `/etc/tmpfiles.d/orbit.conf` rule for `/tmp/orbit-*` and `/dev/shm/orbit-*`; restarts nothing
    SW->>N: Clear Route residue<br/>best effort · Routes steps
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - removes the Caddy sites, PHP pools, certificates, LAN and ingress rules of removed Routes
    %%> - a failure is reported and the part is retried on the next converge; it never fails the task
    %%> Not included:
    %%> - adding or removing a role, and Metrics exporters; those have their own commands
  end
  SW->>N: Check the footprint<br/>exec · sha256sum --check
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - one `sha256sum --check` against the Gateway's hashes: the pinned binary, the recorded key and the agent's `config.toml` and `ca.pem`
  %%> - a missing or mismatched key or file fails this step; `orbit:node-agent-rekey` issues a new key
  %%> Why:
  %%> - a part only counts as applied when the Node shows it; this is the one end check, so there is no separate assert
  %%> Returns:
  %%> - the Gateway reads every step's outcome from Swamp's run data
  alt every part is applied
    N-->>SW: digest per part
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the check passed for every part
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Record footprint digests<br/>Node 12 · task succeeded
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the digest of each applied part, and Node 12's footprint digest
    %%> - the fleet rollout sees Node 12 as up to date
    %%> - task #5132 succeeds
  else a part fails
    N--xSW: exit ≠ 0 or no match
    %%> When:
    %%> - a download doesn't match its pin, the Node agent's key doesn't match, Caddy or PHP-FPM refuse their configuration, or a check fails
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed part
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which part failed and its error code, and which parts finished before it
    Note over GW: Record finished parts<br/>task failed · rerun retries rest
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the digests of the finished parts are recorded; the failed part keeps its old digest
    %%> - task #5132 fails
    %%> On the Node:
    %%> - finished parts stay; there is no rollback
    %%> - the running Node agent keeps its key, so it keeps reporting
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - run the same command again after fixing the cause; it applies only the parts that are still different
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5132
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
  end
